Use superposition (the circuit is linear):
- $v_{in}$ alone ($V_{ref}$ = 0): noninverting, $(1 + R_2/R_1)v_{in}$ = {{(1 + R2/R1)*vin|V}}
- $V_{ref}$ alone ($v_{in}$ = 0): + input grounded, so it is an inverting amplifier for $V_{ref}$: $-(R_2/R_1)V_{ref}$ = {{-(R2/R1)*Vref|V}}
Sum: $v_o$ = {{vo|V}}.
